{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` re-exports 7 names it does not define, each marked\n`# noqa: F401  (re-exported for back-compat)` — 3 from `._processors_identity`\n(`_rederive_keyring_keys`, `process_key_event`, `process_signature`) and 4 from\n`._processors_status` (`_fold_claimed_session`, `_fold_close_metadata`,\n`_fold_plan_review_phase`, `process_status`). ADR 0111 forbids internal shims.\n\nCensused on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d` with an AST pass over `src`, `tests` and\n`scripts` that resolves relative imports and scans `ast.Attribute` and string constants\nseparately. A line-oriented grep undercounts here, because the two densest importers\nspell the name inside a multi-line parenthesized statement.\n\n- **4 names have zero importers** and are deleted outright: `_fold_claimed_session`,\n  `_fold_close_metadata`, `_fold_plan_review_phase`, `_rederive_keyring_keys`. None is\n  used inside `_processors.py` either, so they are dead in both directions.\n- **3 names have importers**, 8 modules in total: `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py:19`\n  (all 3), `test_attestations_reducer.py:13`, `test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:15`,\n  `test_signing.py:117` and `:133`, `test_claimed_session.py:20`,\n  `test_harness_provenance.py:20`, `test_plan_review_phase_happy.py:6`,\n  `test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10`.\n- No attribute-style access anywhere.\n\n**Docs locate these symbols by filename, in a shape no code census can see**, so every\n`_processors*` locator under `docs/` was read directly. Three go stale, and the on-disk\nspelling is two adjacent backtick spans, not one plain string:\n\n- `docs/event-schema.md:234` — ``(`_processors.py` `process_status`)``\n- `docs/event-schema.md:249` — ``(`_processors.py` `_fold_claimed_session`)``\n- `docs/adr/0073-reopen-invalidation-validity-on-read.md:35` —\n  ``(`reducer/_processors.py:process_status`)``, the colon-joined variant.\n\n`docs/event-schema.md:82` shows the target form:\n``reducer/_processors_status.py:_fold_close_metadata``.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Repoint the 3 names that have importers to the modules defining them:\n   `process_key_event` and `process_signature` to `rebar.reducer._processors_identity`,\n   `process_status` to `rebar.reducer._processors_status`.\n2. **Four** importers pull a genuine `_processors` member on the same statement, so they\n   split rather than rewrite wholesale. `_replay.py:19` imports 18 names, 3 of which move\n   — and from two different siblings, so it becomes **three** statements (15 stay).\n   `test_attestations_reducer.py:13` likewise becomes three (`attestation_kind` and\n   `process_snapshot` stay). `test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:15` and\n   `test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10` each also import `process_snapshot` (defined at\n   `_processors.py:469`, stays) — two statements each.\n3. Delete all 7 re-exports. The whole `from ._processors_status import (...)` statement\n   goes, since all 4 of its names are re-export-only. The `._processors_identity`\n   statement keeps `_bootstrap_genesis_keyring` (`:139`, `:520`),\n   `_fold_author_attribution` (`:81`, `:185`, `:296`) and `attestation_kind` (`:508`),\n   which carry no `noqa` because `_processors.py` uses them.\n4. Extend the held-out oracle `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py`, which\n   already covers these modules and sets the convention: assert the re-exports are absent\n   AND that the canonical modules still expose them, so it cannot pass vacuously.\n5. Add a `docs/release-notes.md` entry naming the 3 moved import paths and their new\n   owning module.\n6. Correct the 3 stale doc locators to `reducer/_processors_status.py:<symbol>`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo behavior change: every moved name keeps its definition, only its import path moves.\nThe existing suite is the oracle, with the held-out shim test as the direct assertion.\n`make verify` covers the reducer replay suites that exercise `_replay.py`'s dispatch, the\none production consumer. The doc criteria assert on the **on-disk** spelling, checked\nagainst the tree first, because a grep for a form the file does not use passes vacuously.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `[ \"$(grep -cF 're-exported for back-compat' src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py)\" -eq 0 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC2** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer import _processors as p; assert not any(hasattr(p, n) for n in ['_rederive_keyring_keys','process_key_event','process_signature','_fold_claimed_session','_fold_close_metadata','_fold_plan_review_phase','process_status'])\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer._processors_identity import process_key_event, process_signature; from rebar.reducer._processors_status import process_status\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC4** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer._processors import process_snapshot, attestation_kind\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC5** An AST pass over `src`, `tests` and `scripts` that resolves relative\n      imports finds no `ImportFrom` of `rebar.reducer._processors` naming any of the 7\n      moved names; it exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC6** `ruff check src tests` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC7** `pytest tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py -q` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC8** That file's collected case count is strictly greater than its count on\n      `origin/main`, measured with `pytest --collect-only -q` on both.\n- [ ] **AC9** `[ \"$(grep -cF '`_processors.py` `process_status`' docs/event-schema.md)\" -eq 0 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC10** `[ \"$(grep -cF '`_processors.py` `_fold_claimed_session`' docs/event-schema.md)\" -eq 0 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC11** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'reducer/_processors_status.py:process_status' docs/event-schema.md)\" -eq 1 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC12** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'reducer/_processors_status.py:_fold_claimed_session' docs/event-schema.md)\" -eq 1 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC13** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'reducer/_processors.py:process_status' docs/adr/0073-reopen-invalidation-validity-on-read.md)\" -eq 0 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC14** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'reducer/_processors_status.py:process_status' docs/adr/0073-reopen-invalidation-validity-on-read.md)\" -eq 1 ]`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC15** `docs/release-notes.md` gains an entry naming all 3 moved import paths,\n      and that file's only diff is additions.\n- [ ] **AC16** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly 13 paths:\n      `_processors.py`, `_replay.py`, the 7 named test modules,\n      `test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py`, `docs/release-notes.md`,\n      `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/adr/0073-reopen-invalidation-validity-on-read.md`.\n- [ ] **AC17** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Ordering\n\nIndependent of `insanitary-divine-moa` and `peckish-marmatite-cuckoo` — different\nmodules, no shared file. May land in any order relative to them.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- **`docs/event-schema.md:256`**, ``(`_processors.py` `_clear_claimed_session`)``. Already\n  wrong on `origin/main`: that symbol is defined at `_processors_status.py:35` and was\n  never re-exported. Pre-existing defect; tracked on `icebound-musicianly-parakeet`.\n- **Bare-name prose mentions**, which an import-path move cannot affect:\n  `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:56` and `docs/migrations.md:287`, both naming\n  `process_signature` as a bare symbol rather than a path.\n- **`attestation_kind`**, imported from `_processors` by 5 files (`verify_opcert.py:45`,\n  `_opcert_signing.py:354` and `:437`, `_opcert_verify.py:176`,\n  `test_attestations_reducer.py:13`). Not a re-export — used at `:508` — so it stays.\n- **`test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:63`** captures logs on logger\n  `\"rebar.reducer._processors\"`, emitted at `_processors.py:495` inside\n  `process_snapshot`, which stays. The string must not change.\n- **`_field_contract.py:114`** prose names `rebar.reducer._processors.process_tag_delta`,\n  defined at `_processors.py:434`, which stays.\n- Any behavior change in the processors themselves."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793382706245096851,"uuid":"6d139d1f-ccd5-4223-80c6-1dc47092cd95"}